  "generation": {
    "text": "To determine how many pages Lana has in her binder after receiving pages from Duane, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Identify the number of pages Duane gave to Lana.\n2. Add the number of pages Duane gave to Lana to the number of pages Lana already had.\n\nFirst, we know that Duane took half of the 42 pages in his binder out and gave them to Lana. So, we calculate half of 42:\n\\[\n\\frac{42}{2} = 21\n\\]\nThis means Duane gave 21 pages to Lana.\n\nNext, we add the 21 pages that Duane gave to Lana to the 8 pages that Lana already had:\n\\[\n8 + 21 = 29\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the total number of pages Lana has in her binder after adding Duane’s pages is \\boxed{29}.",
